sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Agent as Coding Agent
    participant Router as "AGENTS.md"
    participant Skills as Peer Skills
    participant CLI as corebase-specharness CLI
    participant Routes as "context-routes.yaml"
    participant Features as "artifacts/features/<slug>/"
    participant Session as ".corebase-specharness/sessions/<slug>/session.md"
    participant Gates as Confirmed Gates
    participant Provider as Optional Review Provider
    participant Memory as Durable Memory

    Agent->>Router: Read portable operating contract
    Agent->>Skills: Invoke a direct peer skill (/spec-*, /harness-*, /context-memory)
    Note over Router,Skills: starter-init is recommended only for an untailored repository

    Skills->>CLI: skill-enter(skill, feature, intent)
    CLI->>Routes: Resolve route, profile, sources, and budget
    CLI->>Features: Create status.md if needed and write enter state
    CLI->>Features: Load route-declared feature artifacts
    CLI->>Session: Create session.md or resume it in place
    CLI-->>Skills: Bounded context pack + operational summary

    opt Focused context refresh / task excerpt
        Skills->>CLI: context-load(skill, feature, task: T-NNN, intent)
        CLI->>Routes: Recompile bounded route context
        CLI-->>Skills: Task-scoped context + retrieved local evidence
    end

    Skills->>Features: Author spec-research / requirements / plan / tasks artifacts
    Skills->>CLI: phase-check and artifact-check where required
    Skills->>CLI: task-check / task-start / task-done / task-block
    CLI->>Features: Validate and update T-NNN task graph, proof, and tasks.json sidecar
    Skills->>Features: spec-implement mutates project source,<br/>tasks.md, and session extracts
    Skills->>CLI: session-checkpoint with progress or handoff
    CLI->>Session: Append progress and handoff updates atomically

    Skills->>CLI: skill-enter(skill: harness-verify, feature)
    CLI->>Features: Write Verifying status
    Skills->>CLI: verify(feature, skill: harness-verify)
    CLI->>Features: Phase readiness, schema, and AC traceability checks
    CLI->>Gates: Run adopter-confirmed argv-safe gates
    Gates-->>CLI: Pass or fail results
    CLI->>Provider: Run selected review action or defer when optional/none
    Provider-->>CLI: Review status and findings
    CLI-->>Skills: verified true/false + mechanical findings
    Skills->>Features: Write review.md after alignment,<br/>design, security, and evidence judgment

    alt Verification passes and verified: true
        Skills->>Features: Record ## Post-Ship Sync in session-extracts.md
        Skills->>CLI: skill-exit(skill: harness-verify, handoff: context-memory)
        CLI->>Features: Set status.md to Done
        Skills->>Memory: Invoke /context-memory
        Memory->>Features: Triage candidate extracts from session-extracts.md
        Memory->>Memory: Promote only evidence-backed durable lessons
    else Verification fails, requests changes, or advisory mode
        Skills->>CLI: skill-exit(skill: harness-verify, phase: ChangesRequested, handoff: spec-implement)
        CLI->>Features: Set status.md to ChangesRequested or Replanning
        Skills->>CLI: session-checkpoint with blockers and next action
        CLI->>Session: Preserve resumable handoff
    end

    Note over Agent,Memory: Skills own procedure, judgment, and artifact authoring.<br/>The CLI owns deterministic context, session, task, artifact, gate, provider, and memory mechanics.
